<sup><b>42</b></sup> On the sixth day Eliasaph the son of Deuel, prince of the children of Gad, <i>offered</i>:<br />
<sup><b>43</b></sup> His offering <i>was</i> one silver charger of the weight of an hundred and thirty <i>shekels</i>, a silver bowl of seventy shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary; both of them full of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat offering:<br />
