<sup><b>51</b></sup> One young bullock, one ram, one lamb of the first year, for a burnt offering:<br />
<sup><b>52</b></sup> One kid of the goats for a sin offering:<br />
<sup><b>53</b></sup> And for a sacrifice of peace offerings, two oxen, five rams, five he goats, five lambs of the first year: this <i>was</i> the offering of Elishama the son of Ammihud.<br />
<sup><b>54</b></sup> On the eighth day <i>offered</i> Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur, prince of the children of Manasseh:<br />
<sup><b>55</b></sup> His offering <i>was</i> one silver charger of the weight of an hundred and thirty <i>shekels</i>, one silver bowl of seventy shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary; both of them full of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat offering:<br />
