<sup><b>59</b></sup> And for a sacrifice of peace offerings, two oxen, five rams, five he goats, five lambs of the first year: this <i>was</i> the offering of Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.<br />
<sup><b>60</b></sup> On the ninth day Abidan the son of Gideoni, prince of the children of Benjamin, <i>offered</i>:<br />
<sup><b>61</b></sup> His offering <i>was</i> one silver charger, the weight whereof <i>was</i> an hundred and thirty <i>shekels</i>, one silver bowl of seventy shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary; both of them full of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat offering:<br />
